274478822947,-0.005454775411635637,-6.675497570540756e-05,-0.00021908267808612436,-0.6648459434509277,-0.6742184162139893,-0.2915602922439575,-1.132075309753418,-0.8643778562545776,-0.22483764588832855,-7.438383181579411e-05,-0.0001699779968475923,-2.3841855067985307e-07,-1.1920928244535389e-07,-1.2966949939727783,-0.2518271207809448,-1.2145733833312988,-0.12160958349704742,-0.23087023198604584,-0.0007933806627988815,-0.0038814221043139696,-1.2859262228012085,-2.333456516265869,-0.025136414915323257,-7.033323527139146e-06,-0.015178651548922062,-0.0017284705536440015],"request":{"active_prefix":"","input_ids":[151644,8948,198,2610,525,1207,16948,11,3465,553,54364,14817,13,1446,525,264,10950,17847,13,151645,198,151644,872,198,50,3948,279,3491,3019,553,3019,13,20678,697,1590,4226,304,1124,79075,90,1112,92,382,10061,400,79,2075,15087,387,264,40899,47311,1741,429,400,79,4080,18,8,284,481,21,4779,400,79,7,19,8,284,220,23,4779,400,79,7,20,8,284,220,16,15,4779,323,400,79,7,22,8,284,220,16,20,2418,220,7379,400,79,7,16,17,568,3,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nLet $p(x)$ be a cubic polynomial such that $p(-3) = -6,$ $p(4) = 8,$ $p(5) = 10,$ and $p(7) = 15.$  Find $p(12).$","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"71139bdb14bb803fe2e2936d0be51c2573319c04479e4cf476e9e968c71abdbf"},"seconds":94.0331597328186,"seed":969446961421493338,"stop":"eos","text":"Given that $p(x)$ is a cubic polynomial, we can write it in the standard form as:\n\\[ p(x) = ax^3 + bx^2 + cx + d \\]\n\nGiven the values $p(-3) = -6,$ $p(4) = 8,$ $p(5) = 10,$ and $p(7) = 15,$ we can set up a system of equations to solve for $a, b, c,$ and $d.$\n\nLet's write down each equation:\n\n1. For $p(-3) = -6$\n\\[ a(-3)^3 + b(-3)^2 + c(-3) + d = -6 \\]\n\\[ -27a + 9b - 3c + d = -6 \\]\n\\[ -27a + 9b - 3c + d = -6 \\quad \\text{(Equation 1)} \\]\n\n2. For $p(4) = 8$\n\\[ a(4)^3 + b(4)^2 + c(4) + d = 8 \\]\n\\[ 64a + 16b + 4c + d = 8 \\quad \\text{(Equation 2)} \\]\n\n3. For $p(5) = 10$\n\\[ a(5)^3 + b(5)^2 + c(5) + d = 10 \\]\n\\[ 125a + 25b + 5c + d = 10 \\quad \\text{(Equation 3)} \\]\n\n4. For $p(7) = 15$\n\\[ a(7)^3 + b(7)^2 + c(7) + d = 15 \\]\n\\[ 343a + 49b + 7c + d = 15 \\quad \\text{(Equation 4)} \\]\n\nWe now have the system of equations:\n\\[\n\\begin{cases}\n-27a + 9b - 3c + d = -6 \\quad \\text{(1)} \\\\\n64a + 16b + 4c + d = 8 \\quad \\text{(2)} \\\\\n125a + 25b + 5c + d = 10 \\quad \\text{(3)} \\\\\n343a + 49b + 7c + d = 15 \\quad \\text{(4)}\n\\end{cases}\n\\]\n\nTo solve for $a, b, c,$ and $d,$ we can subtract equations to eliminate $d.$\n\nSubtracting Equation (1) from Equation (2):\n\\[ (64a + 16b + 4c + d) - (-27a + 9b - 3c + d) = 8 - (-6) \\]\n\\[ 91a + 7b + 7c = 14 \\quad \\text{(Equation 5)} \\]\n\nSubtracting Equation (2) from Equation (3):\n\\[ (125a + 25b + 5c + d) - (64a + 16b + 4c + d) = 10 - 8 \\]\n\\[ 61a + 9b + c = 2 \\quad \\text{(Equation 6)} \\]\n\nSubtracting Equation (3) from Equation (4):\n\\[ (343a + 49b + 7c + d) - (125a + 25b + 5c + d) = 15 - 10 \\]\n\\[ 218a + 24b + 2c = 5 \\quad \\text{(Equation 7)} \\]\n\nNow, we have three new equations:\n\\[\n\\begin{cases}\n91a + 7b + 7c = 14 \\quad \\text{(5)} \\\\\n61a + 9b + c = 2 \\quad \\text{(6)} \\\\\n218a + 24b + 2c = 5 \\quad \\text{(7)}\n\\end{cases}\n\\]\n\nNext, eliminate $c.$ Subtract Equation (6) from Equation (5):\n\\[ (91a + 7b + 7c) - (61a + 9b + c) = 14 - 2 \\]\n\\[ 30a - 2b + 6c = 12 \\]\n\\[ 30a - 2b = 12 \\quad \\text{(Equation 8)} \\]\n\nSubtract Equation (5) from Equation (7):\n\\[ (218a + 24b + 2c) - (91a + 7b + 7c) = 5 - 14 \\]\n\\[ 127a + 17b - 5c = -9 \\quad \\text{(Equation 9)} \\]\n\nMultiply Equation (8) by 5:\n\\[ 150a - 10b = 60 \\quad \\text{(Equation 10)} \\]\n\nNow add Equation (9) and Equation (10):\n\\[ (127a + 17b - 5c) + (150a - 10b) = -9 + 60 \\]\n\\[ 277a + 7b = 51 \\quad \\text{(Equation 11)} \\]\n\nSolve for $a$:\n\\[ 277a = 51 - 7b \\]\n\\[ a = \\frac{51 - 7b}{277} \\]\n\nSubstitute $a$ back into Equation (8):\n\\[ 30 \\left(\\frac{51 - 7b}{277}\\right) - 2b = 12 \\]\n\\[ \\frac{1530 - 210b}{277} - 2b = 12 \\]\n\\[ 1530 - 210b - 554b = 3324 \\]\n\\[ 1530 - 764b = 3324 \\]\n\\[ -764b = 1794 \\]\n\\[ b = -\\frac{1794}{764} = -\\frac{897}{382} \\]\n\\[ b = -\\frac{897}{382} \\]\n\nNow substitute back into Equation (6) to find $c$ and finally $d$.\n\nFinally, substitute $a, b, c,$ and $d$ into the polynomial and evaluate $p(12).$\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{47}\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{47}","correct":false,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
